1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,900
Two exits. One pays the shop.
One pays you back.

2
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,400
There is no third exit.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Layaway worked because you trusted
the shop with the ledger.

4
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:25,600
Apps keep that ledger in a database,
with a withdraw button on top.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:35,400
Bitcoin Cash puts the rule in the money:
a P2SH32 covenant.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:47,400
Target: 10,000 sats. Merchant: fixed.
Start: 2,000 sats, on Chipnet.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:57,400
The invitation is inspectable
before signing.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:07,400
Deposit 11,000: same bytecode,
bigger balance.

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:19,400
Release: merchant gets exactly 10,000.
The extra 1,000 comes back.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,400
Below target: refused by the VM.
Never broadcast.

11
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:40,400
Refund: 3,000 back to the saver,
minus a 2,000 sat fee.

12
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:48,400
One role. Three actions.
Schnorr on every spend.

13
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Layaway, without the middleman.
Chipnet demo · BCH BLAZE 2026
